From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wineopenxr: Preserve external-runtime initialization and Vulkan callbacks.

Rebase the existing external OpenXR runtime support onto Valve's updated
WineOpenXR, keeping its WoW64 callback conversion, checked Unix calls,
session handle mapping, and shared function-availability helper.

Store the host Vulkan function pointer in a fixed-width field shared with
the 32-bit PE loader. A native pointer field would overwrite the following
member when the 64-bit Unix callback is used by a WoW64 application.

The upstream update already fixes handle logging and callback-pointer
casts, so those obsolete hunks are no longer needed.
---

diff --git a/Makefile.in b/Makefile.in
--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -2,4 +2,5 @@
 UNIXLIB    = wineopenxr.so
 IMPORTS    = advapi32 user32 dxgi winevulkan
+UNIX_LIBS  = -lopenxr_loader

 SOURCES = \
